FINDINGS:
1. [BLOCKER] tests/constant_test.rs:179 — `import_binds_a_modules_constants` uses `eval`/`run_isolated` which bypasses `analyzer::analyze`, so it passes while the real `rb run` pipeline (`run_source` lex→parse→analyze→run) rejects `give back TAU` as `Unknown variable` because `Statement::Import` declares nothing — test cannot fail the real path, fake completion — fix by exercising `run_source` and making the analyzer aware of imported names or deferring them to runtime.
2. [BLOCKER] src/analyzer.rs:157 — function bodies are analyzed eagerly at declaration time, so `to f() give back TAU end / constant TAU to ...` reports `Unknown variable` at analyze time, contradicting SPEC.md:667-668 promise that a function body declared above the `constant` reads it too because it runs later — no test covers constant-after-function order — fix with a pre-declaration pass for constants or runtime-only resolution.
3. [BLOCKER] src/bytecode/codegen.rs:163 — `Statement::Constant` compiles to the same `Opcode::Store` as `set`, so duplicate-declaration and `Cannot assign to constant` refusals exist only in the tree-walking VM and a `.rbc` silently rebinds, contradicting SPEC.md:671-672 — fix with a dedicated opcode plus `FORMAT_VERSION` bump or refuse to compile constants until then.
4. [MAJOR] src/vm.rs:294 — `load_module` binds a module `set` via raw `globals.insert`, bypassing the `constants` refusal that `set_var` enforces, so an imported `set` can silently clobber an importer's constant in violation of `No set rebinds a constant` — fix by routing module writes through the same `set_var`/`bind_constant` refusal.
5. [MAJOR] src/vm.rs:298 — `load_module` binds a module `constant` via fallible `bind_constant`, so a second `import MathUtils` in one program errors `Constant 'TAU' is already declared` instead of being idempotent — no test imports twice — fix by making re-import a no-op when the name is already bound to the same module value.
REVIEW VERDICT: FINDINGS 5
